# RED-PROOF + GREEN — W5 merged search surface unit suite

Suite: web/test/search-groups.test.ts (16 tests)
Covers: the pure core of the §7.3 merged search surface — group order and labels, the
catalog-fence mapping (lexicons pinned as its own register query), URL-state parsing/building
(query, E8 include-personal default-OFF, group collapse, per-group paging offsets with clamps),
and the ILIKE/excerpt text helpers. The per-group query fan-out itself (S-12) is pinned against
the real engine by web/test/invariants/search-register-groups.test.ts (W2, separately logged).

## RED RUN (watched fail first)

Four simultaneous mutations to web/src/lib/search-groups.ts:
  M1a PERSONAL_GROUPS reversed (design order violated)
  M1b include-personal defaulted ON (E8 "explicit" violated)
  M2a offset clamp [0, SEARCH_MAX_OFFSET] removed (the search-sections.ts `?offset=1e21` scar)
  M2b collapsed-id filter dropped (unknown ids admitted into URLs)

Command: cd web && npx vitest run test/search-groups.test.ts   → exit 1, 6 failed | 10 passed

Failing tests:
  - §7.3 group model > order (M1a)
  - parseSearchState > defaults to include-personal OFF (M1b)
  - parseSearchState > only personal=1 counts (M1b)
  - parseSearchState > offsets clamped (M2a)
  - parseSearchState > unknown collapsed ids dropped (M2b)
  - buildSearchHref > round-trips (M2a/M2b: mutated state no longer round-trips)

